Wear comfortable, breathable clothing during workouts. Proper underwear can also help keep the pad securely positioned.

Hydration is important during exercise regardless of whether you are menstruating. Drink enough water based on your activity level and environment.

Nutrition is another part of supporting an active lifestyle. Include carbohydrates for energy, protein for normal body functions, and a variety of fruits and vegetables.

If your period is extremely heavy and exercise regularly causes dizziness or unusual fatigue, it is important to speak with a healthcare professional. Heavy bleeding can sometimes be associated with low iron levels.

There is no need to feel embarrassed about exercising while menstruating. Periods are a normal biological process, and many people continue their normal routines during menstruation.

The key is flexibility. On days when you feel energetic, you may continue your regular workout. On days when you experience discomfort, gentle movement or rest may be more appropriate.

Pay attention to your body and choose the activity level that feels right for you.
